From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(instance): pin device/process/kernel policy override
 arms (batch 3)

### What
Pins the third batch of `apply_override_inner` match arms: `contract.devices.read/.write/.create`, `contract.process.signals` and `contract.kernel.proc_read` each apply their parsed list to the matching field, and a non-empty device create list flips `filesystem_device_nodes`.

### Why it matters
Each arm is an independent security-policy channel. A deleted arm silently ignores the operator's override while returning success, so a device or kernel rule would never take effect. The existing suite pins batch 1 (#370) and the filesystem batch (#385) but not these five arms.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| delete `contract.devices.read` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `contract.devices.create` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `contract.process.signals` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `contract.kernel.proc_read` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-instance --lib override_policy_channels`.

Spec-Ref: ginux instance-config override contract (device/process/kernel policy channels)

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
index cfb78bd5..8f6937af 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
@@ -3251,4 +3251,27 @@ failure = "stop"
             .unwrap();
         assert_eq!(c.contract_deny.as_slice().len(), 1);
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn override_policy_channels_devices_process_kernel_apply_exactly() {
+        let mut c = InstanceConfig::parse(VALID.as_bytes()).unwrap();
+        c.apply_override(b"contract.devices.read", b"[\"/dev/null\"]")
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.device_read.as_slice().len(), 1);
+        assert_eq!(c.device_read.as_slice()[0].as_bytes(), b"/dev/null");
+        c.apply_override(b"contract.devices.write", b"[\"/dev/zero\"]")
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.device_write.as_slice().len(), 1);
+        c.apply_override(b"contract.devices.create", b"[\"/dev/custom\"]")
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.device_create.as_slice().len(), 1);
+        assert!(c.filesystem_device_nodes);
+        c.apply_override(b"contract.process.signals", b"[\"signal.kill\"]")
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.process_signals.as_slice().len(), 1);
+        c.apply_override(b"contract.kernel.proc_read", b"[\"/proc/**\"]")
+            .unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.kernel_proc_read.as_slice().len(), 1);
+        assert_eq!(c.kernel_proc_read.as_slice()[0].as_bytes(), b"/proc/**");
+    }
 }
